      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TREPORTI (2) is a local veteran resuming from a spell, and he has been placed 6 times from 11 starts fresh up in the past. The bar plates are off his front hooves for the first time, which has to be a positive, and from a good draw, he might just sneak a win. PROVANCE (3) dropped in class, and found some good form when running on from last to finish second here 2 weeks ago, albeit in a 6-horse field. He is nicely placed again from a superior draw, and another solid effort can be expected. FIGHTING IDOL (6) was doing his best work late fresh up at the Sunshine Coast over 1000m, and the extra 110m will suit him. Each way. JEMELDI (4) was a touch plain last start, but he is better than that, and is worth another chance.",
